      "sourceText": "The fire in the hearth of the Crooked Stag crackled with a dry woodsmoke scent that was far less welcome than the rain outside. Elias Thorne stood on the tavern’s flagstone floor, his leather armor feeling heavier than usual after weeks of travel. He adjusted the strap of his sword hilt and looked toward the table where the village elder sat. The man had cleared a small space on the scarred wooden surface for the contract scroll, which lay open alongside a heavy iron purse that caught the lantern light.\n\nElias folded his hands behind his back, keeping his posture loose but ready. ",
